    "status": "pending",
    "exactTargets": [
      "iPhone SE (3rd generation)",
      "iPhone 16 Pro Max"
    ],
    "runtime": "the highest available iOS 26.x simulator runtime",
    "procedure": "Resolve one exact device type before device selection. Existing and created devices must have that type identifier and a canonical 36-character hyphenated hexadecimal UUID. Ignore a same-name wrong-type device. Select one highest available iOS 26.x runtime before target resolution. Ignore exact targets in older runtimes. Accept one exact available target only in the selected runtime. Fail when that runtime has more than one exact available target. Otherwise, create the target once from the exact device type in the selected runtime. Then poll unfiltered simctl list devices -j snapshots for no more than 30 seconds at one-second intervals. Give each poll subprocess only the remaining verification time. On a poll timeout, retain the partial snapshot and final verification log, then fail closed. Locate the returned canonical UUID across all runtime records. Accept one available record only when it has the selected runtime key, exact target name, and exact device type. Retain device-type, runtime, pre-creation device, creation, poll snapshot, final verification, and resolution logs.",
    "failure": "Fail on an absent or ambiguous exact device type, an invalid matching UUID, no available iOS 26.x runtime, invalid or ambiguous highest-version selection, multiple exact available targets in the selected runtime, creation failure, a poll subprocess timeout, a duplicate returned UUID, a wrong runtime, name, or device type, a missing record at the deadline, an unavailable record at the deadline, or ambiguous exact resolution. Do not create the target again."
  },
